description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts. Three exact string replacements, all in pickMostLandable. Use the strings verbatim; do not re-derive anchors. Each occurs exactly once in the file (verified). Verified to typecheck cleanly with all three applied.

REPLACEMENT 1
old:
  const actionableGaps: Record<string, unknown>[] = [];
new:
  const actionableGaps: Record<string, unknown>[] = [];
  // RE-TEST PATH (2026-08-28). The comment above promises "penalty, not hard exclusion",
  // but this branch used a bare `continue`, which DELETED the category from selection.
  // An excluded category can never record a land, because updateCalibration(cat, true)
  // fires only at gap CLOSURE and an unpickable gap never closes — so lands === 0 is both
  // the cause and the effect. Hold them back instead and use them when nothing else is
  // available, which is what the comment above already describes.
  const hopelessGaps: Record<string, unknown>[] = [];

REPLACEMENT 2
old (three lines, indentation exactly as shown — six spaces, four spaces, four spaces):
      continue;
    }
    actionableGaps.push(g);
new (four lines):
      hopelessGaps.push(g);
      continue;
    }
    actionableGaps.push(g);

REPLACEMENT 3
old:
  const scoredGaps = actionableGaps;
new:
  const scoredGaps = actionableGaps.length ? actionableGaps : hopelessGaps;

Nothing else changes. Do not touch the hopeless() predicate itself, the uiQuestion_write escalation, the impact-ranking code below, or any other function.

WHY: the comment directly above hopeless() states the intended design — "strongly deprioritise gaps in a category the substrate has EMPIRICALLY learned it cannot land (>=8 attempts, 0 lands) ... while leaving a re-test path (penalty, not hard exclusion) if nothing better exists." The code does the opposite: a bare `continue` removes the gap from the candidate list entirely. That is self-sealing, because updateCalibration(category, true) is called only at the two gap-CLOSURE sites, so a category that cannot be picked can never close a gap, can never record a land, and therefore can never stop satisfying lands === 0. Measured on the live calibration file: 12 categories sit at >= 8 attempts with 0 lands, and every gap-to-feature pick line reports hopeless_excluded between 40 and 80.

This is the third self-sealing mechanism found today; the other two were repaired in vessel-mitosis-evaluate.ts (17aae9a) and vessel-mitosis-cutover.ts (cf28f52), and both immediately restored autonomous landing.

The change is conservative: hopeless gaps are still deprioritised to last resort and the human escalation still fires unchanged. They become selectable only when the actionable list is empty, which is precisely the "if nothing better exists" the comment already promises.

